WEBVTT

00:47.440 --> 00:49.690
<b>May, Unified Year 1927</b>

00:52.070 --> 00:55.070
<b>The Empire's Unstoppable March Continues...</b>

01:20.720 --> 01:24.060
<b>You're out of your office in 
the middle of an operation, huh?</b>

01:24.360 --> 01:26.780
<b>And you're entering without permission.</b>

01:28.560 --> 01:31.150
<b>Does the word "classified" 
mean nothing to you?</b>

01:31.150 --> 01:35.340
<b>I simply thought you might 
join me for breakfast.</b>

01:36.610 --> 01:38.700
<b>You stayed here all night again?</b>

01:38.960 --> 01:42.570
<b>There's no one waiting for me at home.</b>

01:42.570 --> 01:46.210
<b>Your wife and daughter are still 
at her parents' home in the south?</b>

01:46.440 --> 01:50.200
<b>Yes. They haven't left since 
my daughter's fiancé died.</b>

01:50.520 --> 01:53.760
<b>It's still badly affecting her, it seems.</b>

01:54.650 --> 01:57.250
<b>I'm sure she knew it was possible, but...</b>

01:57.670 --> 02:01.480
<b>It's a tragedy happening everywhere 
in the Empire right now.</b>

02:05.810 --> 02:08.770
<b>You can come stay at 
my place, if you like.</b>

02:09.320 --> 02:11.920
<b>I'll get you something more 
comfortable to sleep on.</b>

02:11.920 --> 02:13.010
<b>I'll pass.</b>

02:13.010 --> 02:15.100
<b>As long as I can sleep, it 
doesn't matter where I do it.</b>

02:16.260 --> 02:18.950
<b>The operation's started.</b>

02:18.950 --> 02:22.490
<b>A large-scale counterattack that 
will determine the fate of the war.</b>

02:23.780 --> 02:28.000
<b>However it ends, I hope it ends here.</b>

02:29.530 --> 02:30.950
<b>Yes.</b>

04:02.090 --> 04:06.600
<b>This story is a work of fiction. People, organizations, locations, laws, names, etc. have no relation to any real-life counterparts.</b>

04:03.710 --> 04:04.860
<b>How does our comms network look?</b>

04:04.860 --> 04:05.700
<b>It's fine.</b>

04:05.700 --> 04:07.320
<b>No sign of enemy airpower in the area.</b>

04:06.670 --> 04:11.610
<b>"No reparations, no territorial changes, 
no other conditions" is not acceptable.</b>

04:11.610 --> 04:13.660
<b>That's our leaders' determination.</b>

04:14.030 --> 04:19.170
<b>Which means we need to win 
better terms for ourselves.</b>

04:19.170 --> 04:21.740
<b>Security guarantees are our top priority.</b>

04:21.740 --> 04:27.250
<b>A demilitarized buffer zone. 
And reparations, if possible.</b>

04:27.250 --> 04:30.130
<b>It's fine to continue 
the negotiations, but...</b>

04:30.130 --> 04:32.340
<b>Now the war's entirely political.</b>

04:32.340 --> 04:35.030
<b>High leadership made the call.</b>

04:35.030 --> 04:37.450
<b>I'm sure you have your own 
opinions as a soldier,</b>

04:37.450 --> 04:39.220
<b>but I'll ask you to 
keep them to yourself.</b>

04:39.580 --> 04:40.940
<b>It's time.</b>

04:46.340 --> 04:49.350
<b>Episode Four
Operation Iron Hammer</b>

04:46.700 --> 04:48.670
<b>Let's get started, then.</b>

04:56.670 --> 04:59.060
<b>A sealed order from command.</b>

05:00.370 --> 05:03.940
<b>Now, let's see what 
they've got to say today...</b>

05:06.740 --> 05:09.790
<b>Paratroopers? That's crazy.</b>

05:09.790 --> 05:11.790
<b>The bridges are too far...</b>

05:12.320 --> 05:15.490
<b>Get our officers together immediately.</b>

05:15.490 --> 05:16.630
<b>Understood.</b>

05:19.880 --> 05:22.820
<b>We still don't have our lines 
in good order...</b>

05:22.820 --> 05:26.970
<b>Even if we push our lines forward, 
they'll just push them back.</b>

05:26.970 --> 05:29.930
<b>We still don't have enough supplies...</b>

05:30.460 --> 05:33.610
<b><i>This was supposed to end 
with unconditional peace!</i></b>

05:33.610 --> 05:36.380
<b><i>And instead we're launching 
a large-scale attack?</i></b>

05:36.780 --> 05:41.720
<b>Major, what should I be doing 
during this operation?</b>

05:41.720 --> 05:45.330
<b>Don't worry. Nothing difficult.</b>

05:45.330 --> 05:47.050
<b>If they tell you to go, you go.</b>

05:47.050 --> 05:48.800
<b>If they tell you to return, you return.</b>

05:48.800 --> 05:52.280
<b>You run around for a while, 
and then the battle's over.</b>

05:54.220 --> 05:58.710
<b><i>Our trained officers have learned to 
keep their heads straight, but...</i></b>

05:59.150 --> 06:02.330
<b>If you're going to fight, 
you need sweets!</b>

06:02.330 --> 06:04.520
<b>Hey, don't keep them to yourself!</b>

06:06.720 --> 06:09.530
<b>Hey, don't take every last one!</b>

06:09.530 --> 06:12.910
<b><i>I'll have to take a lesson from them.</i></b>

06:12.910 --> 06:16.060
<b><i>It's not like peace talks 
are off the table entirely.</i></b>

06:16.060 --> 06:18.710
<b><i>I'll just have to do my job.</i></b>

06:20.450 --> 06:22.440
<b>It's time, everyone!</b>

06:23.960 --> 06:28.450
<b>Our goal for this operation is to surround
and annihilate the enemy's field army.</b>

06:28.450 --> 06:31.010
<b>We'll destroy the enemy's main forces</b>

06:31.010 --> 06:34.190
<b>and eliminate their ability 
to continue this war.</b>

06:34.840 --> 06:40.040
<b>The key to this operation is to use the 
river to the enemy's rear as a barrier.</b>

06:40.700 --> 06:45.540
<b>The paratroopers have already 
deployed to make this happen.</b>

06:45.910 --> 06:48.530
<b>They're attempting to lock 
down several bridges.</b>

06:49.070 --> 06:53.230
<b>We will follow up and 
reinforce the paratroopers,</b>

06:53.230 --> 06:55.750
<b>destroying the enemy's line 
of retreat and supply lines.</b>

06:56.200 --> 06:59.720
<b>Of course, the enemy will do whatever 
it takes to get those bridges back.</b>

07:00.320 --> 07:04.240
<b>We need to support the paratroopers 
and protect the bridges.</b>

07:04.830 --> 07:08.070
<b>Thus, this operation 
will be about mobility.</b>

07:08.070 --> 07:12.170
<b>We will smash into the enemy lines 
with a highly mobile "iron hammer"</b>

07:12.170 --> 07:14.790
<b>and meet up with our paratroopers 
at the enemy's rear.</b>

07:14.790 --> 07:17.760
<b>With their lines of retreat 
and supplies totally cut off,</b>

07:17.760 --> 07:20.310
<b>we will then divide and surround 
the enemy field army.</b>

07:20.310 --> 07:24.920
<b>Our allies will then 
annihilate our trapped foe.</b>

07:25.270 --> 07:29.320
<b>So thoroughly the Federation's leadership
never wants to fight a war again.</b>

07:30.170 --> 07:34.170
<b>Our job in this operation is to 
be at the front of the charge.</b>

07:34.510 --> 07:36.480
<b>We'll be breaking through 
the enemy's center.</b>

07:37.010 --> 07:40.230
<b>If we're delayed, the paratroopers 
may be wiped out.</b>

07:40.230 --> 07:42.120
<b>Our responsibility is great.</b>

07:43.650 --> 07:47.780
<b>Lieutenant Colonel, an operation 
like this requires air superiority.</b>

07:47.780 --> 07:50.900
<b>We can't move when 
we're being shot from the sky.</b>

07:50.900 --> 07:52.470
<b>Don't worry.</b>

07:52.470 --> 07:55.810
<b>Our allies have already secured 
air superiority, I'm told.</b>

07:55.810 --> 07:59.000
<b>Even if that's true, 
the enemy's defenses are strong.</b>

07:59.000 --> 08:01.680
<b>They don't have any trenches yet, but...</b>

08:01.680 --> 08:03.380
<b>How do we break through?</b>

08:04.000 --> 08:05.880
<b>Look at this!</b>

08:08.320 --> 08:12.280
<b>A Federation command jurisdiction map?</b>

08:12.280 --> 08:13.330
<b>That's right.</b>

08:13.330 --> 08:15.860
<b>Strategic HQ intelligence 
has a plan for us</b>

08:15.860 --> 08:18.870
<b>to slip through the gaps in 
their assigned combat areas.</b>

08:19.700 --> 08:23.690
<b>But can we slip through the enemy's 
lines with an entire division?</b>

08:23.690 --> 08:25.840
<b>Is that possible?</b>

08:25.840 --> 08:28.670
<b>We won't be able to communicate 
with our allies, right?</b>

08:28.670 --> 08:31.230
<b>I can understand your concerns.</b>

08:31.230 --> 08:34.030
<b>So I've decided to 
prepare a little trick.</b>

08:34.340 --> 08:36.970
<b>A trick, ma'am?</b>

08:38.530 --> 08:41.230
<b>That's correct, Captain Ahrens.</b>

08:41.490 --> 08:46.360
<b>Get us to the river, 
no matter what it takes.</b>

08:48.750 --> 08:53.200
<b>Sitting on a tank hurts my butt 
more than I thought it would.</b>

08:53.200 --> 08:54.810
<b>It sure does.</b>

08:54.810 --> 08:58.700
<b>But it means we don't give off any 
magical signals like we do when we fly,</b>

08:58.700 --> 09:02.270
<b>so the enemy will be focusing 
on the other mage units.</b>

09:02.530 --> 09:06.270
<b>The Federation will be looking for 
mages in the sky, not on the ground.</b>

09:06.270 --> 09:09.120
<b>And that means we're much 
more likely to succeed.</b>

09:09.120 --> 09:11.630
<b>We have clear visibility on 
any approaching enemies too.</b>

09:13.480 --> 09:15.030
<b>Enemy attack!</b>

09:15.480 --> 09:16.890
<b>3 o'clock!</b>

09:21.820 --> 09:24.860
<b><i>We're completely within enemy territory.</i></b>

09:24.860 --> 09:26.530
<b><i>If the enemy finds us...</i></b>

09:27.020 --> 09:29.920
<b><i>We're sitting ducks.</i></b>

09:40.810 --> 09:42.300
<b>Hang on tight!</b>

10:31.990 --> 10:34.260
<b>Ambush at one o' clock!</b>

10:38.300 --> 10:40.060
<b>W-Wait, don't shoot!</b>

10:41.060 --> 10:42.490
<b>Those helmets!</b>

10:42.490 --> 10:43.670
<b>Those are allies!</b>

10:43.670 --> 10:45.160
<b>Our allied paratroops.</b>

10:45.530 --> 10:48.290
<b>Everyone! Wave your helmets! Wave them!</b>

10:55.210 --> 10:56.590
<b>Comrades!</b>

10:56.590 --> 10:58.030
<b>I'm so glad you're alive!</b>

10:58.030 --> 11:00.340
<b>I'm so glad you're here!</b>

11:00.790 --> 11:04.430
<b>I'm Lieutenant Colonel Degurechaff,
formerly in charge of this combat team.</b>

11:04.810 --> 11:06.700
<b>Is there anything you need?</b>

11:06.700 --> 11:10.840
<b>We've been here for three days 
and are running low on ammo.</b>

11:10.840 --> 11:12.610
<b>I'll get it immediately.</b>

11:12.610 --> 11:16.600
<b>We'll ask for some water in exchange.</b>

11:16.600 --> 11:18.160
<b>Water?</b>

11:18.730 --> 11:20.730
<b>There's plenty of water...</b>

11:20.730 --> 11:23.600
<b>That's what you've won as 
a prize of war, right?</b>

11:24.830 --> 11:28.660
<b>Let's have a trade, then. Water for ammo.</b>

11:29.340 --> 11:32.330
<b>True. This is our war prize.</b>

11:33.020 --> 11:35.690
<b>I'll take a photograph to 
remember the occasion later.</b>

11:35.690 --> 11:39.070
<b>Of course. Let us prepare the cameras!</b>

11:39.840 --> 11:41.110
<b>The charge was a success.</b>

11:41.110 --> 11:44.800
<b>6th Airborne Regiment has made contact 
with the Rerugen Combat Team.</b>

11:44.800 --> 11:47.010
<b>The Rerugen Combat Team?</b>

11:47.010 --> 11:48.040
<b>Apologies.</b>

11:48.040 --> 11:50.550
<b>That's the codename for 
the Salamander Combat Team.</b>

11:50.800 --> 11:53.330
<b>Let's surround the enemy 
immediately with all our forces.</b>

11:53.330 --> 11:55.570
<b>The troops have already started to move.</b>

11:55.570 --> 11:57.560
<b>Okay, we've got them.</b>

11:57.560 --> 11:59.620
<b>This is where the mission really begins.</b>

11:59.620 --> 12:02.050
<b>We'll stop the enemy's 
attempt to break out.</b>

12:02.050 --> 12:06.580
<b>Taking out their counterattack unit's
leadership would be the fastest way.</b>

12:06.580 --> 12:08.960
<b>Attack their HQ directly?</b>

12:08.960 --> 12:11.670
<b>Which unit has resources
to spare for that?</b>

12:11.670 --> 12:13.820
<b>Don't play dumb, Zettour.</b>

12:14.280 --> 12:19.830
<b>We have the perfect hunting dog for 
this job just waiting around in the East.</b>

12:20.630 --> 12:21.830
<b>Them?</b>

12:22.390 --> 12:23.840
<b>Indeed.</b>

12:27.090 --> 12:29.150
<b>The enemy's camp is better 
defended than we thought!</b>

12:29.150 --> 12:30.770
<b>None of the units are making progress!</b>

12:30.770 --> 12:34.860
<b><i>Damn it... Strategic HQ 
never gives me a day off!</i></b>

12:34.860 --> 12:36.150
<b>We're pulling back!</b>

12:36.150 --> 12:38.270
<b>Major Weiss! Casualty report!</b>

12:38.270 --> 12:39.670
<b>Eight lightly wounded!</b>

12:39.670 --> 12:42.930
<b>The most badly wounded is an idiot 
who took a bullet in the behind!</b>

12:42.930 --> 12:44.990
<b>We're capable of continuing 
the operation!</b>

12:44.990 --> 12:47.140
<b><i>We are not!</i></b>

12:47.140 --> 12:50.760
<b><i>There's no reason for us to work 
so hard for some random side job!</i></b>

12:53.250 --> 12:55.620
<b>There's a possibility of 
enemy reinforcements.</b>

12:55.620 --> 12:57.140
<b>We're retreating.</b>

12:57.800 --> 13:00.910
<b>And even if we did break through 
their camp and find their HQ,</b>

13:00.910 --> 13:03.400
<b>we don't know for sure that 
it would really be their HQ.</b>

13:03.800 --> 13:05.640
<b>I don't know if I follow...</b>

13:05.960 --> 13:08.510
<b>It's likely they've set up a fake HQ.</b>

13:08.510 --> 13:10.080
<b>So this is a trap.</b>

13:10.080 --> 13:12.020
<b>It's obviously a trap.</b>

13:12.020 --> 13:15.260
<b>Or are we supposed to be bulls 
charging at a red piece of cloth?</b>

13:16.540 --> 13:22.620
<b>If we were lucky enough to find the 
enemy HQ, would it really be their HQ?</b>

13:22.620 --> 13:23.820
<b>Really?</b>

13:24.160 --> 13:27.340
<b>Thus, we will maintain our 
anti-surface formation</b>

13:27.340 --> 13:30.060
<b>and continue to hunt for the enemy 
HQ, just in the opposite direction.</b>

13:30.060 --> 13:31.480
<b>The opposite direction!</b>

13:34.920 --> 13:37.640
<b><i>It's important to always do your job,</i></b>

13:37.640 --> 13:40.520
<b><i>but only when there's 
enough in it for you.</i></b>

13:39.230 --> 13:41.330
<b><i>Eight o' clock! I found it!</i></b>

13:41.860 --> 13:43.010
<b>What?</b>

13:43.950 --> 13:45.250
<b>Enemy command!</b>

13:45.600 --> 13:47.040
<b>I'm sure of it!</b>

13:47.040 --> 13:49.900
<b>H-He found it?</b>

13:49.900 --> 13:52.330
<b>That moron has made so many bad IDs!</b>

13:52.330 --> 13:54.060
<b>Why does he have to be right now?</b>

13:54.940 --> 13:58.600
<b>Lieutenant Colonel, 
it's time for us to be bulls, right?</b>

14:00.150 --> 14:01.480
<b>Fuck it all!</b>

14:05.240 --> 14:06.760
<b>Attention all units!</b>

14:06.760 --> 14:09.570
<b>Any units in the vicinity of 
the enemy camp and command HQ</b>

14:09.570 --> 14:10.870
<b>are to evacuate immediately!</b>

14:10.870 --> 14:12.320
<b>Hurry!</b>

14:14.770 --> 14:17.070
<b>Damn it all!</b>

14:20.480 --> 14:22.110
<b>Direct hit on enemy command!</b>

14:22.110 --> 14:24.660
<b>The Rerugen Combat Team has done it!</b>

14:28.720 --> 14:32.290
<b>We were just beginning to see the enemy 
make an organized attempt at escape.</b>

14:32.290 --> 14:36.220
<b>We managed to stop them from escaping.</b>

14:36.670 --> 14:40.110
<b>That's the best we can 
hope for now, I believe.</b>

14:41.100 --> 14:45.610
<b>Everyone, we've done it!</b>

14:45.610 --> 14:47.450
<b>Lieutenant General Rudersdorf!</b>

14:47.450 --> 14:49.070
<b>Congratulations!</b>

14:47.830 --> 14:49.620
<b>We've won.</b>

14:50.180 --> 14:51.610
<b>Yes.</b>

14:51.960 --> 14:53.900
<b>Once more, we were able to win.</b>

15:05.280 --> 15:07.720
<b>Oh, Lieutenant Colonel Degurechaff.</b>

15:07.720 --> 15:10.460
<b>Hello, Colonel Calandro.</b>

15:10.460 --> 15:12.740
<b>Marvelously done.</b>

15:12.740 --> 15:16.800
<b>After a defeat like that, it's only a matter
of time before a ceasefire is signed.</b>

15:16.800 --> 15:21.800
<b>But I'm told we allowed 
an organized retreat in several places.</b>

15:21.800 --> 15:24.680
<b>Well, you can't be 
expected to get 'em all.</b>

15:24.680 --> 15:28.790
<b>Either way, the war will continue 
until peace is achieved.</b>

15:29.260 --> 15:30.700
<b>Sheesh...</b>

15:31.000 --> 15:33.480
<b>It's good to not let your guard down.</b>

15:35.020 --> 15:38.980
<b>Why don't the two of you take 
a picture to celebrate?</b>

15:39.700 --> 15:42.460
<b>No, I'll pass.</b>

15:42.460 --> 15:43.960
<b>It's your nation that won the day.</b>

15:44.450 --> 15:45.290
<b>Fare well.</b>

15:48.040 --> 15:50.540
<b>Lieutenant Colonel, make a pose!</b>

15:51.010 --> 15:53.250
<b>Give me a more natural smile!</b>

15:53.800 --> 15:55.180
<b>A little more!</b>

15:55.180 --> 15:56.280
<b>Grin!</b>

15:55.520 --> 15:57.090
<b>Grin...</b>

15:59.940 --> 16:03.190
<b>Does this make up 
for my sins at least a little?</b>

16:17.910 --> 16:22.320
<b>It won't be long until 
you make field marshal.</b>

16:22.320 --> 16:27.170
<b>I appreciate it, but the honor is 
something to be shared among us all.</b>

16:27.170 --> 16:30.400
<b>No, it's clear who was 
taking the lead here.</b>

16:30.810 --> 16:33.660
<b>My friend, you've done it.</b>

16:33.660 --> 16:35.390
<b>Be proud.</b>

16:36.840 --> 16:39.050
<b>Should I say thank you?</b>

16:40.030 --> 16:43.060
<b>To me? To the soldiers?</b>

16:43.680 --> 16:45.820
<b>The soldiers, I suppose.</b>

16:46.550 --> 16:50.580
<b>Now, even Moskva is 
within reach of our troops.</b>

16:52.580 --> 16:55.060
<b>Only in theory.</b>

16:56.050 --> 16:59.050
<b>The lack of supplies is a problem?</b>

16:59.870 --> 17:02.860
<b>We've little hope of bringing 
the railways back online.</b>

17:02.860 --> 17:05.960
<b>The ceasefire negotiations 
should be our top priority.</b>

17:06.270 --> 17:10.830
<b>I just got the report in 
from Colonel Rerugen.</b>

17:10.830 --> 17:13.480
<b>It's only a matter of time 
before it's reached.</b>

17:13.480 --> 17:16.920
<b>The Federation is putting 
together a peace proposal.</b>

17:16.920 --> 17:17.970
<b>Excuse me.</b>

17:17.970 --> 17:19.470
<b>News for you both.</b>

17:19.470 --> 17:22.570
<b>High leadership is holding 
an emergency meeting.</b>

17:25.480 --> 17:28.520
<b>We still have some forces left,</b>

17:28.520 --> 17:30.730
<b>but this is a disaster.</b>

17:30.730 --> 17:34.190
<b>I can understand why the Politburo 
wants to end the war, but...</b>

17:34.430 --> 17:37.870
<b>I'm supposed to give up 
on my beautiful fairy?!</b>

17:43.060 --> 17:44.380
<b>Oh?</b>

17:45.040 --> 17:48.170
<b>Oh? Oh? Oh?</b>

17:51.540 --> 17:55.510
<b>Demands Are Overwhelmingly One-Sided</b>

17:51.840 --> 17:54.530
<b>The Empire is drunk on victory?</b>

17:54.530 --> 17:56.610
<b>They're falling for their own propaganda,</b>

17:56.590 --> 17:59.550
<b>Massive Reparations</b>

17:56.610 --> 17:59.230
<b>without knowing what things 
are really like for them?</b>

17:59.550 --> 18:04.440
<b>This is why the masses need 
to be properly led.</b>

18:05.540 --> 18:08.940
<b>We must fight this war politically.</b>

18:08.940 --> 18:13.940
<b>When you're in love, 
everything goes your way.</b>

18:13.940 --> 18:15.940
<b>Empire High Leadership Building</b>

18:15.950 --> 18:20.190
<b>An immediate ceasefire 
along existing lines.</b>

18:20.190 --> 18:25.810
<b>Areas currently under our control 
will remain so.</b>

18:25.810 --> 18:28.950
<b>A demilitarized zone will exist for 
several kilometers along the border.</b>

18:28.950 --> 18:31.680
<b>Citizens in presently occupied territories</b>

18:31.680 --> 18:34.940
<b>will be given the opportunity to 
vote for independence or join us.</b>

18:34.940 --> 18:36.920
<b>We will accept multinational observers,</b>

18:36.920 --> 18:39.450
<b>and the vote will be held as soon 
as the peace agreement is signed.</b>

18:39.450 --> 18:43.470
<b>This is the peace agreement the military
 and the Ildoa Kingdom put together?</b>

18:43.470 --> 18:46.250
<b>Yes, that's right.</b>

18:48.310 --> 18:52.990
<b>You're really trying to tell me 
this agreement is in our favor?</b>

18:52.990 --> 18:54.220
<b>What?</b>

18:54.220 --> 18:55.620
<b>Indeed.</b>

18:55.620 --> 19:00.230
<b>The military believes this is the best 
deal we can get and supports it.</b>

19:00.230 --> 19:03.870
<b>I'm sorry, but can you really call 
yourself an Imperial officer?</b>

19:04.170 --> 19:06.450
<b>How can we have peace 
with these awful conditions?</b>

19:06.450 --> 19:08.010
<b>"Awful conditions"?</b>

19:08.010 --> 19:13.450
<b>Many of our men died to make 
the enemy agree to them.</b>

19:13.450 --> 19:17.050
<b>It seems you're unaware of 
domestic political opinion.</b>

19:17.050 --> 19:21.410
<b>We can't have a ceasefire or 
peace with these conditions.</b>

19:21.410 --> 19:24.310
<b>The Empire has suffered 
massive financial damage.</b>

19:24.310 --> 19:26.730
<b>Without reparations, our budget will...</b>

19:26.730 --> 19:28.400
<b>You'll go bankrupt, I assume.</b>

19:28.690 --> 19:31.500
<b>The government itself may fall.</b>

19:31.500 --> 19:35.070
<b>And while I hesitate to say it,</b>

19:35.560 --> 19:38.950
<b>the Imperial family itself 
may be in danger.</b>

19:38.950 --> 19:41.950
<b>You overstep, sir.</b>

19:41.950 --> 19:45.440
<b>A soldier should fear only 
one thing: his enemy!</b>

19:45.710 --> 19:49.590
<b>If too much fear of a civil war 
puts the whole nation in danger,</b>

19:49.590 --> 19:51.460
<b>then isn't it better to have a civil war?</b>

19:52.880 --> 19:55.030
<b>Lieutenant General Rudersdorf.</b>

19:55.030 --> 19:58.450
<b>This operation was yours, 
so I'd like to hear your opinion.</b>

19:58.450 --> 20:02.960
<b>Do you believe the Imperial Army 
cannot win any more victories?</b>

20:04.060 --> 20:07.980
<b>To be honest, it will be difficult.</b>

20:07.980 --> 20:09.470
<b>"Difficult"?</b>

20:09.870 --> 20:12.650
<b>Indeed. Difficult.</b>

20:12.650 --> 20:14.970
<b>You're not saying impossible, I see.</b>

20:15.580 --> 20:20.730
<b>A soldier's job is to protect the 
nation from external threats.</b>

20:21.020 --> 20:25.750
<b>Many soldiers have sacrificed their 
lives to bring us to this point.</b>

20:26.060 --> 20:29.750
<b>I don't know if it's worth 
sacrificing more of them.</b>

20:30.100 --> 20:33.750
<b>But if you're willing to make 
unlimited sacrifices...</b>

20:34.350 --> 20:38.260
<b>How could I be so irresponsible 
as to say we cannot win?</b>

20:38.710 --> 20:43.500
<b>So you're saying if we're willing to 
take the needed measures for victory,</b>

20:43.500 --> 20:45.510
<b>we may be able to win?</b>

20:46.730 --> 20:50.510
<b>Then we must have you fight 
for the future of our nation.</b>

20:50.510 --> 20:53.730
<b>No matter how many of our men must die?</b>

20:53.730 --> 20:56.330
<b>We can't let our sacrifices 
so far be in vain.</b>

20:56.330 --> 20:59.530
<b>So we must be prepared to make more.</b>

21:02.310 --> 21:04.040
<b>Very well.</b>

21:09.850 --> 21:11.030
<b><i>Stop it.</i></b>

21:11.030 --> 21:13.540
<b>If you insist so much on victory...</b>

21:13.860 --> 21:15.040
<b><i>Don't!</i></b>

21:15.040 --> 21:17.240
<b>...then I shall bring you victory!</b>

21:17.240 --> 21:21.340
<b><i>Shut your mouth, Rudersdorf!</i></b>

21:23.330 --> 21:26.220
<b>No matter what the cost...</b>

21:27.350 --> 21:32.060
<b>Our army shall be victorious!</b>

23:14.490 --> 23:16.320
<b>All right, I'll take the photo!</b>

23:30.930 --> 23:32.100
<b>Huh?</b>

23:32.500 --> 23:34.120
<b>Why?</b>

23:36.260 --> 23:40.090
<b>Next Time
Unlucky Draw</b>
